From: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa2-lite: reassert global filtering before uplink TX

The IPA v2.6L hardware returns uplink packets to the AP route with the
FILT_PROCESS status bit clear even though the modem table is installed and
its pointer is valid.  The modem/uC setup can clear the global IPA_FILTER
register after the AP has populated its filter table.

Reassert the global filter-enable bit immediately before sending an AP
producer packet.  This is the same bit programmed by downstream's
ipa_cfg_filter(false), and doing it at the producer boundary makes the
ordering independent of the asynchronous Q6 data-call setup.

Signed-off-by: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
index 20f4900..0f3cf2b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
@@ -1930,6 +1930,14 @@ static netdev_tx_t ipa_ndev_start_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb,
 		if (ret == 2)
 			return NETDEV_TX_BUSY;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Q6/uC setup may clear IPA_FILTER after tables have been installed.
+	 * This is the AP producer boundary, so restore the downstream global
+	 * enable bit immediately before IPA consumes the packet.
+	 */
+	if (ipa_ndev->tx && ipa_ndev->tx->id == EP_TX)
+		iowrite32(1, ipa->mmio + REG_IPA_FILTER_OFST);
+
 	if (skb->protocol != htons(ETH_P_MAP) || skb_linearize(skb) || !ipa_ndev->tx)
 		goto drop_tx;
